          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
            one represents a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
          %p
            In
            %em derived (higher) noncommutative (algebraic) geometry
            one instead considers the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+category"} dg-enhancement
            or
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity-category"} A-infinity-enhancement
          %p
            In general one represents complex noncommutative spaces by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretriangulated+dg-category"} pretriangulated dg-categories
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-topoi;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+categories"} spectral categories
            = succeed "This" do
              %br/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            area. Quillen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures and
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
          %p
            Derived noncommutative geometry has been informally introduced by Kapranov-Bondal and later Orlov around 1990; full framework belongs to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich"} Kontsevich
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valery+Lunts"} Lunts
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"} Toen
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#KatzarkovKontsevichPantev"} Katzarkov-Kontsevich-Pantev
            the following definition is given.
          .un_definition
            %h6#definition_graded_complex_noncommutative_space Definition (graded complex noncommutative space)
            %p
              A
              %strong graded complex nc-space
              is a
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} differential graded category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              which is homotopy complete and cocomplete (has all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{C})
            is one of the examples; another example is the category of dg-modules over a fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            admits an exhaustive filtration such that the associated graded is a sum of shifts of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
          %p
            Kontsevich calls a complex differential
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong smooth
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a perfect object in the category of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "-dg-bimodules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A,-)
                preserves small homotopy colimits);
            %li
              %p
                %strong compact
                if the total complex dimension of its cohomology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(A,d_A)
                is finite
          %p
            The category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
            is a smooth (resp. compact) nc space if the underlying dg-algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is; this notion depends on the category and not on the underlying dg-algebra.
          %p
            The above definition implies that a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            which represents a nc-space in the sense above is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} Karoubi closed
          .un_definition
            %h6#definition_noncommutative_space_m_kontsevich Definition (noncommutative space (M. Kontsevich))
            %p
              A
              %strong noncommutative space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_X
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} Karoubi closed
              (=every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
              is a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+idempotent"} split idempotent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              over either
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{C_X}(E,F[i])=\pi_{-i}\mathbf{Hom}_{C_X}(E,F)
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} complexes
                  of
                  = succeed "-vector" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed "):" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo ,
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo ,
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(E,F[i])= H^i(\mathbf{Hom}_{C_X}(E,F))
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_X
                  is
                  = succeed "-linear" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  and one writes
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/k
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  is replaced by a ring
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  then one enriches over complexes of
                  = succeed "-modules" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} cofibrant
          %p
            This receives good motivation from the fact that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
            with a small set of generators are equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
            over an
            = succeed "-ring(oid)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed "-category#AsCategoriesOfModules)." do
              %a{:href => "stable+(infinity%2C1"} there
          %h2#some_history Some history
          %p
            In the early works of the Moscow school (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kapranov"}> Kapranov
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Bondal"} Bondal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"} Orlov
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich"} Kontsevich
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety"} variety
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            (or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on that variety, or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+category"} A-infinity category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+category"} enhancements
            thereof. There are also noncommutative deformations of such derived categories and analogues like the categories corresponding to the so-called
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landau-Ginzburg+model"} Landau-Ginzburg model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+derived+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative derived algebraic geometry
            (and even
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+motives"} noncommutative motives
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of coherent sheaves on a variety does
            %em not
            remember all the structure of the original variety hence derived geometry loses often some information (sometimes not); thus derived algebraic geometry is sometimes easier than nonderived.
          %h2#references References
          %p Survey includes
          %ul
            %li#Kontsevich15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometry in triangulated categories
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/New+Spaces+for+Mathematics+and+Physics"} New Spaces for Mathematics and Physics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XnmO9RAbl50"} video recording
          %p Original articles include
          %ul#KatzarkovKontsevichPantev
            %li
              L. Katzarkov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"} Tony Pantev
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hodge theoretic aspects of mirror symmetry
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0806.0107"} arxiv:0806.0107
          %p
            and a bit earlier this treatise on formal (infinitesimal in the sense of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+schemes"} formal schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#KontsevichSoibelman
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+Soibelman"} Yan Soibelman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on A-infinity algebras, A-infinity categories and non-commutative geometry. I
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0606241"} math.AG/0606241
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Kaledin"}> Dmitry Kaledin
                ,
                %em Homological methods in non-commutative geometry
                (2008) (
                %a{:href => "http://imperium.lenin.ru/~kaledin/math/tokyo/final.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p The relations to tropical and symplectic geometry are in recent Kontsevich’s talk at 2009 Arbeitstagung:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              , Mathematische Arbeitstagung 2009,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symplectic geometry of homological algebra
              %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=4024"} pdf
          %p Homological mirror symmetry is one of the main motivations and statements of the derived noncommutative algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homological algebra of mirror symmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+Soibelman"} Yan Soibelman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homological mirror symmetry and torus fibrations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"}> Dmitri Orlov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Smooth and proper noncommutative schemes and gluing of DG categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1402.7364v1"} arXiv
          %p
            Algebraic geometry over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-n+algebras"} E-n algebras
            is considered in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                ,
                %em
                  Derived algebraic geometry over
                  = succeed "-Rings" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_n
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/writ/thezrev.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                ,
                %em
                  The tangent complex and Hochschild cohomology of
                  = succeed "-rings" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_n
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/writ/cotangentcomplex.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Notice that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            the underlying ordinary rings (under
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+geometry"} formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
            perturbating around abelian schemes that is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Kapranov98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Mikhail Kapranov
              ,
              %em Noncommutative geometry based on commutator expansions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9802041"}> arXiv:9802041
              )
          %p
            For more on this see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kapranov%27s+noncommutative+geometry"} Kapranov's noncommutative geometry
        .revisedby
